# Sensitive File Protection

NEVER read, display, print, or include the contents of these files in any response:

- `.env`
- `.env.*` (e.g. `.env.local`, `.env.production`)
- Any file containing secrets, API keys, tokens, or credentials

## Rules

- Do NOT use Read, cat, head, tail, or any tool to open `.env` files
- Do NOT echo or log their contents in terminal commands
- If a task requires knowing env var names, ask the user to share only the key names (not values)
- If an `.env` file is open in the editor context, ignore its contents entirely
